  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday Night through next Friday)\nIssued at 1130 AM CDT Fri Jul 10 2026\n\nThe wet pattern lingers into early next week as a broad upper-\nlevel ridge builds to the west, helping to cut off or slow a low\nover the TN Valley. A west-east oriented boundary will drift\nslowly south, sustaining chances for scattered showers and \nstorms, particularly during the afternoon/evening hours. Heavy \nrain and localized flooding remain possible through Monday. \n\nBy mid to late week, the upper ridge expands over the region,\nleading to drier overall conditions with only isolated afternoon\nstorms. Temperatures will remain warm and humid, with highs\ngenerally in the upper 80s to low 90s and lows in the upper 60s to\nlow 70s. Overall, rain chances drop significantly by end of next\nweek, offering some relief from the ongoing flood risk.",
